/ Stage 4 (ruling 8): `set %x% = '{"a":1}' as json` lands %x% as `{text, kind: json}`
/ per decision 749 + ruling 1 (name stays parent, sub-sort rides as kind). Red today —
/ the baseline is dict 5/5; %x!type.name% reads "dict" (not "text"), so the first assert
/ fails before the kind can be checked.
AsJsonKeepsJson
- set %x% = "{\"a\":1}" as json
- assert.equals(Expected="text", Actual=%x!type.name%, Message="type.name is text")
- assert.equals(Expected="json", Actual=%x!type.kind.name%, Message="type.kind.name is json")
